      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2015, American College of Rheumatology.",
        "AbstractText": [
          {
            "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
            "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
            "content": "Although the Computer Assisted Management in Early Rheumatoid Arthritis Trial-II (CAMERA-II) showed favorable clinical effects in the most intensive methotrexate (MTX)-based strategy with prednisone (MTX\u2009±\u2009prednisone) compared to that with placebo (MTX\u2009+\u2009placebo), this beneficial difference was only seen in 1 of the 3 analyses of remission. Our objective was to investigate whether the Continuity Rewarded (ConRew) score and a simple sum score would better reveal differences regarding remission between the 2 treatment arms of CAMERA-II. Furthermore, we investigated whether the patient vector graph, which plots on patient level, would add visual information on remission compared to a conventional box plot only, which displays data on the group level."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "METHODS",
            "content": "The ConRew method, which awards continuous periods of remission with a higher score, was applied, in addition to a simple sum score of remission periods of 4 weeks. A patient vector graph was compared with box plots."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
            "Label": "RESULTS",
            "content": "Both the mean\u2009±\u2009SD simple sum score and the ConRew score of remission were significantly higher (favorable) in the MTX\u2009+\u2009prednisone strategy group versus the MTX\u2009+\u2009placebo group, respectively: 9\u2009±\u20097 versus 12\u2009±\u20098; P\u2009=\u20090.003, and 23\u2009±\u200916 versus 17\u2009±\u200914; P\u2009=\u20090.004. The patient vector graphs show a visual pattern of more and longer periods of remission in the MTX\u2009+\u2009prednisone strategy and visually add information to the box plots."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "Label": "CONCLUSION",
            "content": "The simple sum of remission periods, the ConRew score, and the patient vector graph add understanding and discrimination to the analysis of the remission outcome in CAMERA-II."
          }
        ]
      },
